M(TS,"Which is safest for typing a JSON API response at a trust boundary?",["Validate at runtime (e.g. Zod) and infer the type from the schema","Cast with `as`","Use any","Trust the server docs"],"Casting doesn't check anything at runtime.");
M(TS,"What's the difference between `void` and `undefined` as return types?",["void means the return value is ignored; undefined must be returned","They are identical","void must return null","undefined means no return at all"],"A callback typed () => void may return any value that the caller ignores.");
S(TS,"Which are built-in utility types?",["Partial","Required","Pick","NonNullable"],["DeepPartial","Mutable","Optionalize"],"Deep variants must be written yourself or imported from a library.");
S(TS,"Which are erased at runtime (no JavaScript emitted)?",["interface","type alias","generic parameters","type annotations"],["class","regular enum","const declarations"],"Classes and enums produce runtime code.");
S(TS,"Which help narrow a union type?",["typeof checks","instanceof","in operator","discriminant property checks"],["as any","@ts-ignore"],"Casts and ts-ignore bypass rather than narrow.");
W(TS,"When would you use `type` over `interface` and vice versa?",[["union","intersection","tuple","mapped"],["extend","merge","declaration merging"],["consistent","convention","object shape","public api","class"]],"Use type for unions, tuples, mapped/conditional types and aliases of primitives. Use interface for object shapes you want to extend/merge (public library APIs, class contracts); interfaces give clearer errors and cache better. Many teams pick one by convention and be consistent.");
W(TS,"Explain generics and give a realistic example.",[["reusable","parameter","placeholder","type variable"],["constraint","extends"],["fetch","api","hook","list","array","identity","response"]],"Generics parameterise types so a function or component works with many types while preserving relationships between inputs and outputs, e.g. function first<T>(xs: T[]): T | undefined, or an API client get<T>(url): Promise<T>. Constraints (T extends X) restrict what T can be.");
W(TS,"How do you type-safely handle an exhaustive switch on a union?",[["never"],["discriminant","kind","tag","type field"],["compile","error","missing case"]],"Switch on a discriminant, and in default assign the value to a `never` variable (or call assertNever). If a new union member is added without a case, the compiler errors.");
W(TS,"What TS compiler options do you consider essential in a strict project?",[["strict"],["noimplicitany","strictnullchecks","noUncheckedIndexedAccess","exactOptionalPropertyTypes","noImplicitReturns"],["isolatedmodules","skiplibcheck","moduleresolution","target"]],"Turn on `strict`, plus noUncheckedIndexedAccess, noImplicitOverride and noImplicitReturns; set isolatedModules for bundler compatibility, a modern moduleResolution (bundler/nodenext), skipLibCheck for speed, and verbatimModuleSyntax for import hygiene.");
