W(RC,"Compare Context, Redux/Zustand and server-state libraries like TanStack Query.",[["context","small","theme","low-frequency","re-render"],["redux","zustand","global","client state","store"],["server state","cache","query","stale","refetch"],["selector","devtools","boilerplate"]],"Context is fine for low-frequency values (theme, auth) but re-renders all consumers. Redux/Zustand manage complex client state with selectors and devtools. Server state (fetched data) belongs in a library like TanStack Query that handles caching, deduping, refetching, staleness and mutations. Mixing the concerns is the main mistake.");
