W(RC,"Controlled vs uncontrolled components: when do you pick each?",[["controlled","state","value","onchange"],["uncontrolled","ref","defaultvalue","dom","formdata"],["validation","dynamic","simple","performance","file input"]],"Controlled inputs keep their value in React state, ideal for live validation, formatting and dependent fields. Uncontrolled inputs let the DOM hold state and are read via refs/FormData, which is simpler and cheaper for basic forms and file inputs. Form libraries mix both for performance.");
