W(SD,"Compare polling, long-polling, SSE and WebSockets.",[["polling","interval","repeated"],["long","hold","open until"],["sse","server-sent","one-way","unidirectional"],["websocket","bidirectional","full-duplex","two-way"],["proxy","reconnect","scale","firewall"]],"Polling repeats requests (simple, wasteful). Long-polling holds a request open until data is available. SSE is a one-way server-to-client stream with auto-reconnect over HTTP. WebSockets are bidirectional and low latency but need connection management and scaling. Pick by direction and frequency.");
